C. Hand Calculation – Series RLC Circuit Given:

Resistance (R=10\ \Omega)
Inductive reactance (X_L=5\ \Omega)
Capacitive reactance (X_C=10\ \Omega) The individual impedances are: [ Z_R=10+j0 ]
[ Z_L=0+j5 ]

[ Z_C=0-j10 ]

Total series impedance: [ Z=Z_R+Z_L+Z_C ]

[ Z=10+j5-j10 ]

[ \boxed{Z=10-j5\ \Omega} ]

Magnitude: [ |Z|=\sqrt{10^2+(-5)^2} ]

[ \boxed{|Z|=11.18\ \Omega} ]

D. Hand Calculation – Parallel RLC Circuit Using: [ Z_p=\frac{Z_1Z_2}{Z_1+Z_2} ]

First, combine resistor and inductor: [ Z_{RL}=\frac{10(j5)}{10+j5} ]

[ Z_{RL}=2+j4 ]

Now combine this with the capacitor: [ Z_p=\frac{(2+j4)(-j10)}{(2+j4)-j10} ]

[ Z_p=\frac{40-j20}{2-j6} ]

[ \boxed{Z_p=5+j5\ \Omega} ]

Magnitude: [ |Z_p|=\sqrt{5^2+5^2} ]

[ \boxed{|Z_p|=7.07\ \Omega} ]

Both calculated results match the program's expected output. E. Division by zero test The program attempts: Complex zero(0, 0); Complex result = a / zero;

