Evaluation: The custom class is useful for understanding constructors and operator overloading. std::complex is more suitable for real-world applications because it is standardized, reusable and already tested. 7. Conclusion The Complex class was successfully designed and implemented using constructors and operator overloading. The program performs addition, subtraction, multiplication, division and equality comparison. It also calculates series and parallel RLC circuit impedance and displays the magnitude of the results.

The division-by-zero test demonstrates safe exception handling. The comparison with std::complex shows that a custom class provides learning and design control, while the standard library offers a simpler solution for practical applications.
